<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parion</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parion was an ancient Greek city on the Asian shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellespont">Hellespont</a>, near the village of Kemer in Çanakkale province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. Founded in the 8th or 7th century BCE by colonists from Paros, Miletus and Erythrae, it prospered from trade through the straits and later became a Roman colony. Excavations since 2005 have uncovered its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, odeon and necropolis.</p></div>
